			"Message": "style(Common): Clean up remaining HTML entity spacing in badges and heading\n\nThe prior commit introduced `&#x2001;` entities to fix Unicode em-space rendering, but left some placements where a plain space is sufficient — the badge row gaps are wide enough without an em space, and the section heading reads better with normal spacing.\n\nRemove `&#x2001;` from the two Crates.io badge lines (replacing with regular space) and from the \"System Architecture\" heading (replacing with regular space). This produces tighter, more natural spacing in these locations while the em-space entity remains in use elsewhere in the document where explicit separation is visually required.",
